1
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,120
<i>Are you sure if we put on an act,</i>

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,240
<i>the ghost will be</i>
<i>stupid enough to believe us?</i>

3
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,680
You just have to make it convincing enough
for it to believe us.

4
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,880
You usually look so dead inside
when talking to clients.

5
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,440
<i>What's gotten into you, Vann?</i>

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,880
From now on, if you're sad, look at this
bracelet and think of me instead.

7
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,240
<i>You don't have to think about anyone else.</i>

8
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,240
<i>Rakkhun.</i>

9
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,560
We're still together, right?

10
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,280
Kan came to talk to me.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,000
<i>What do you think I should do?</i>

12
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:32,840
<i>Why are you scared?</i>

13
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:35,480
<i>The ghost… is the one</i>
<i>who should be scared of me.</i>

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:42,800
You're leaving already?

15
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,920
If that's all you're going to do,
don't bother coming.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,000
What a waste of time.

17
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,520
Vann! What are you doing?

18
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:50,520
Aw!

19
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,040
I thought you'd be scarier than this.

20
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,680
Come out and let me see you if you dare.

21
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:54,800
Don't just make noises.

22
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,160
And did you turn off the lights
to boost the damage?

23
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:58,920
It's not scary at all.

24
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,720
Save that trick for scaring kids.

25
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,920
Rakkhun.

26
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,960
How about we go public as a couple?

27
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,200
And when you graduate, we'll get married.

28
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:18,440
Vann. What's wrong with you?

29
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,360
Took you long enough to show yourself.

30
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,800
You kept me waiting so long.

31
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,640
Get out.

32
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,560
Where do you expect me to go?

33
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:34,440
You're choking me.

34
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,640
Go die wherever you want.

35
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,600
What are you saying?

36
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,040
I can't understand you.

37
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,360
What's your name? What do you want?

38
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,560
Tell me.

39
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,600
You have to stay away from Rakkhun.

40
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,040
Otherwise, I'll kill you.

41
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:55,160
Vann!

42
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,360
What happened?

43
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,560
I'm scared.

44
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:06,120
Tell him that Garlah will kill you.

45
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,360
Vann. Are you okay?

46
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:20,720
I'm fine. I'm okay.

47
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,360
Don't worry about me.

48
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:23,920
Your neck.

49
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,320
Your neck.

50
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,320
You really won't go to the hospital?

51
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:34,720
I can take you.

52
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,120
No.

53
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,880
Just take care of me. That's enough.

54
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,240
Don't even start.

55
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,400
How could you provoke her like that?

56
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:47,840
What if she really snapped your neck?

57
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,560
What would you do?

58
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,240
Come on.

59
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,520
My neck didn't come off.

60
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:58,360
At least now I know her name is Garlah.

61
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,240
It was worth it.

62
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,960
You risked that much just
to learn her name?

63
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,200
How does knowing that help you?

64
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:08,440
At least the fact that
Garlah showed herself to me

65
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:11,080
means she believes we're together.

66
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,960
Now you don't have to worry.

67
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,400
I'll talk to her.

68
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,079
You'll definitely get
to live the life you want.

69
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,720
But go to sleep now.

70
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,760
I'll keep working on the model.

71
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,720
I can't sleep.

72
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,320
The knife is still stuck in the model.

73
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,720
Seriously, Vann.

74
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,360
I don't want to sleep here at all.

75
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:35,400
Didn't you say
she could follow you anywhere?

76
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,000
That's right.

77
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,600
But I can't sleep.

78
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,760
If it's somewhere else,
you'll be able to sleep, right?

79
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,760
Come in.

80
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,600
Whoa.

81
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,480
Are all these yours?

82
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,280
Yeah.

83
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:10,160
I saved up and bought them myself.

84
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:12,080
Some of them have been discontinued.

85
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,840
You're such a nerd.

86
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,120
Whoa.

87
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,640
Hey!

88
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,480
You can look, but don't touch.
They might break.

89
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,640
These things are delicate.

90
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,040
Wow. You're really protective of them.

91
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,600
Of course I am.

92
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,120
Each one was so hard to get.

93
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,680
Some of them almost ended up at the dump.

94
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:37,800
Luckily, I got to them in time.

95
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,800
Go shower and get some sleep.

96
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,320
You sleep on the bed tonight.

97
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,840
I'll sleep on the floor.

98
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,000
No.

99
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,440
You sleep on the bed.

100
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,680
I'll sleep on the floor.

101
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:50,000
No way.

102
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:54,720
I have to take good care of
my super VVIP client.

103
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,440
Go take a shower.

104
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,520
Go, go, go!

105
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,640
Fine, I'll go.

106
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,360
Sorry.

107
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:26,080
I'll lower it for you.

108
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,560
Is the light bothering your eyes?

109
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:02,040
Should I move somewhere else
to work on it?

110
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:05,640
It's fine.

111
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,200
I can't sleep anyway.

112
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,520
Want me to help?

113
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:19,840
Didn't you tell me you'd be able
to sleep somewhere else?

114
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:24,000
I do feel more at ease here
than in my room.

115
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,440
But I feel bad if you do it alone.

116
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,200
I'm chill. Don't overthink it.

117
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,080
This is my job.

118
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,080
Once this job is done, I get paid.

119
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,480
See? It's a win-win for both of us.

120
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,680
Hey, did I say something wrong?

121
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,680
No.

122
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,120
Can I ask you something?

123
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,960
Why did you join the Crow Club?

124
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,080
I don't really want to use this word, but…

125
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,840
I guess it was fate.

126
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,920
My life was terrible back then.

127
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,040
I got fired.

128
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:13,320
And I didn't get the scholarship.

129
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:16,320
But I happened to meet Linda.

130
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,200
When Linda offered me a job at the club,

131
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:25,280
at first, I wondered
what kind of job paid this much.

132
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,240
But I had nothing left to lose.

133
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:31,520
As long as I could earn money legally,
I'd do any job.

134
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:34,080
And it really does pay a lot.

135
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,880
Even if the jobs are a little weird.

136
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,559
Oh, you…

137
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,600
When you're ready to sleep,
you fall asleep so easily.

138
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,200
Why am I smiling?

139
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,600
Damn it!

140
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:49,000
Your face is so red. Are you okay?

141
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,720
And why are you sleeping here?

142
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,400
Someone fell asleep last night.

143
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,160
And then…

144
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:01,320
you held my hand and wouldn't let go.

145
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,400
"Stay here. Don't leave me."

146
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,520
You're exaggerating.

147
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:15,000
Didn't you put your hand in mine yourself
and then make the whole thing up?

148
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,040
There's a camera in my room.

149
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,600
Want me to pull up the footage?

150
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,720
No need.

151
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,120
I'm going to take a shower.

152
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,320
I'm not talking to you anymore.

153
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,480
Hey, that's the blanket.

154
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:30,440
Where are you taking it?

155
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,480
Yeah.

156
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,440
Hurry up and shower.

157
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:43,840
I'll take you to get something to eat.

158
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:51,640
Mimi, can I have another chicken thigh?

159
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,040
There's only one chicken thigh.

160
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,160
You had the chicken thigh
the other day too.

161
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:57,080
- Hey, how could you do this?
- We're eating.

162
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,640
Can I have some too?

163
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,040
What's there to eat today?

164
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,360
Look. Can't you see?

165
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,440
Whoa!

166
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,560
Linda made a lot of food today.

167
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,080
Is she planning to feed
the whole neighborhood?

168
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,760
Sit down.

169
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:15,840
What? What are you guys looking at?

170
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,760
Hey.

171
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,560
If you're going to go public,

172
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,360
shouldn't you introduce him first?

173
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,040
He gets here and you just let him sit?

174
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,160
Hi, nice to meet you.

175
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:31,120
I'm Mimi.

176
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,400
Hi, I'm Rakkhun.

177
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,760
You can call me Rak.

178
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,520
Rakkhun?

179
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,720
Your name is so unique.

180
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:40,920
I can't believe someone
as foul-mouthed as Vann

181
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,880
could actually have a boyfriend.

182
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:45,200
Not a boyfriend. He's a client, damn it.

183
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,440
Is he really our client?

184
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:52,720
He's our client?

185
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,440
- Come here.
- What?

186
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,800
You brought a client to sleep at the club?

187
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:05,440
Why did Linda never tell us
we could do that?

188
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:06,920
I would've done it too.

189
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:09,720
Vann. Are you crazy?

190
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,360
Did you forget Linda's golden rule?

191
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,400
Yeah, Vann.

192
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,840
If any Crow crosses the line

193
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:18,440
and gets so involved with a client
that they can't separate the two,

194
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,200
they'll be kicked out.

195
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:21,960
You guys are getting carried away.

196
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:24,520
I brought him here because of work.

197
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:27,200
And I already got Linda's permission.

198
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,440
And she gave you permission?

199
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,480
She's playing favorites.

200
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:35,120
I'm sorry, everyone, for disturbing you.

201
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,280
I might be staying here for a while.

202
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,240
Until Vann finishes this job.

203
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:43,800
You don't have to apologize, Rakkhun.

204
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:47,000
Having another handsome guy join our club,

205
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:50,240
I'm more than happy about it.

206
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,480
Are you tired? Did you travel far?

207
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:54,080
- I'm not tired.
- If you're tired, eat plenty.

208
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,080
Go on, eat. Here, I'll feed you.

209
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,280
Make yourself at home, Rakkhun.

210
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,200
The Crow Club welcomes you.

211
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,400
Thank you.

212
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:05,720
Since you've moved in here,

213
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,680
does that mean you've seen the ghost?

214
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:10,000
I have.

215
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,600
Her name is Garlah.

216
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,800
But that was as far as
our conversation got.

217
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:16,280
- She disappeared first.
- Shit!

218
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:19,880
Vann. You talk to everyone
from people to ghosts now?

219
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:24,080
If you guys want to know how this
will turn out, have Nay read the cards.

220
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:26,320
I'm not doing that. It's nonsense.

221
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,160
Reading the cards won't change anything.

222
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,760
You guys know how to read cards too?

223
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,560
Interested?

224
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:34,120
If you are, I can read the cards for you.

225
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,880
I am.

226
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,160
Come on. Let's do it after we eat.

227
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:40,920
Eat up.

228
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,240
Your boyfriend is superstitious.

229
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,760
I told you, he's not my boyfriend.

230
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,120
What do you want to do? Go ahead.

231
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,520
Who is the ghost following me?

232
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:02,040
Looks like she's been around
for a very long time.

233
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:06,040
She could be your ancestor
or someone who's watching over you.

234
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,400
When she appeared,

235
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:10,560
judging by the way she was dressed,

236
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:12,480
she must've been your Yong ancestor.

237
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:14,680
Yong?

238
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,240
- Ramyun?
- No.

239
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:20,640
So what does she want?

240
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,840
She won't tell us.

241
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,400
If I make merit for her,
will she stop following me?

242
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,720
She won't tell us.

243
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,440
And she covered the cards
so we couldn't see them.

244
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,520
Vann.

245
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,040
You've only seen her once?

246
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,160
Yeah, I've only seen her once.

247
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:56,000
But it took so much to get her to appear.

248
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:59,120
Maybe next time,
I'll actually have to kiss Rakkhun.

249
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,040
- A kiss?
- A kiss?

250
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:00,960
Come on, Vann.

251
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,240
Like, kiss-kiss?

252
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,000
It's a long story.

253
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,400
I'll tell you later.

254
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,320
But I need to find
a way to talk to her first.

255
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:12,200
Does she have to be
the one to come to you?

256
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:17,280
If I don't wait for her to appear,
what do you expect me to do?

257
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,240
Go out and find her?

258
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,080
I don't want to die yet.

259
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:25,240
We don't have to go find her.

260
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:28,280
Because we can summon her.

261
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,720
How?

262
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,440
Do you have her number?

263
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,840
You want him to call the ghost?

264
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,440
Is this how you summon a ghost?

265
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,200
Yes.

266
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:48,480
My family usually performs this ritual
at the ancestral spirit shrine.

267
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:49,800
Then the ghost appears.

268
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,040
Didn't you say you've never seen a ghost?

269
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,520
I've never seen one directly.

270
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,640
But I've seen one through a spirit medium.

271
00:15:57,560 --> 00:16:00,840
Usually, one person in my family
is chosen to be the spirit medium.

272
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,800
And everyone in the family can talk to
our ancestors through them.

273
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,920
If the ghost appears here,
who'll be the medium?

274
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:16,360
If the ghost appears, you can see her.

275
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,120
So we don't need a medium.

276
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:22,320
Hey! Do we have to light incense too?

277
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,840
Of course. The incense is important.

278
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,480
Fine, light it.

279
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,040
But be careful.
Don't let anything catch fire.

280
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:32,760
Or all my dinosaurs will go extinct.

281
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,600
What should I do?

282
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:36,640
I forgot the chant.

283
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,440
Will the ghost even appear?

284
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,600
I'm not usually the one who chants.

285
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,760
Then who usually does it?

286
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,440
Can you call and ask them?

287
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,240
My grandmother.

288
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,240
But I've recorded her before.

289
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:54,040
Because my mother once made me
memorize this chant.

290
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:01,560
<i>Sacred beings of the northern skies.</i>

291
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:04,599
- I'll transcribe it and try chanting it.
<i>- Please open the path between worlds.</i>

292
00:17:05,839 --> 00:17:06,880
By the time you're done,

293
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,560
we'll probably be chanting it next month.

294
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,760
Then what would you do?

295
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:11,760
Just have your grandmother chant it.

296
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:15,040
You mean play the recording
and perform the ritual at the same time?

297
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:16,960
This is the age of technology.

298
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,400
Your ancestors…

299
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,079
They probably won't mind.

300
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:27,839
<i>Sacred beings of the northern skies,</i>

301
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,280
<i>please open the path between worlds.</i>

302
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:32,920
<i>Let the voices of the descendants</i>
<i>reach the departed.</i>

303
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:35,360
<i>Om, spirits of the household,</i>

304
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:38,360
<i>spirits of the family line, elders,</i>

305
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,120
<i>forefathers and foremothers,</i>

306
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,840
<i>those who once built homes,</i>

307
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:45,320
<i>worked the fields, planted rice,</i>

308
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,200
- Do you see a ghost?
<i>- and raised children.</i>

309
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:48,720
- No.
<i>- Now…</i>

310
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,920
- I don't see anything.
<i>- We will light incense.</i>

311
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,760
<i>May you hear this voice</i>
<i>from wherever you are.</i>

312
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,800
- I don't think it's working.
<i>- Please come down to this house</i>

313
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,560
- If she were coming, she'd be here by now.
<i>- to receive</i>

314
00:17:58,640 --> 00:17:59,640
- Pack it up.
<i>- the offerings,</i>

315
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,840
Wait.

316
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:04,480
- Can you wait until the incense burns out?
<i>- including food and water.</i>

317
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,280
She's here.

318
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,880
Garlah is here.

319
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:17,720
I don't think that's her.

320
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:19,800
What kind of ghost has such good manners?

321
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,480
It even knocked first.

322
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:27,040
Linda sent me to ask if you guys
are having dinner together.

323
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,960
I am. An army marches on its stomach.

324
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:31,240
Tell her to make some for me.

325
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:33,720
You guys aren't done yet?

326
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,200
Almost.

327
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:46,920
What do you want to do?

328
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,200
You want to wait until
the incense burns out, right?

329
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,280
I don't think this method
is really going to work.

330
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,360
Are you that disappointed?

331
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:58,440
A little.

332
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,440
I've dealt with things like
this my whole life.

333
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:04,000
I don't want to put up with this anymore.

334
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,440
Do you trust me?

335
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:10,960
I do.

336
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:14,400
Otherwise, I wouldn't have
pestered you into taking the job.

337
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,440
Then let me apologize in advance.

338
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,760
Nothing's happening.

339
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,760
Wait, Vann.

340
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:27,880
She's here.

341
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,160
It actually worked.

342
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,960
- Hey, you!
- Stay right there.

343
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:36,680
Hey, you. I thought you weren't coming.

344
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:38,840
You're pretty naughty, aren't you?

345
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:40,280
Incense doesn't work on you,

346
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:42,360
but the moment we kissed, you showed up.

347
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:46,160
But thank you for not losing your temper
and throwing a knife at us like last time.

348
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,960
Vann, how can you provoke her like that?

349
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:50,320
You'll get hurt again.

350
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:52,320
Trust me.

351
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:54,320
Just watch a pro at work.

352
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,000
I'll get straight to the point.

353
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,880
My eyes get tired
just looking at you and your bug eyes.

354
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:02,560
My Rakkhun here

355
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:06,240
wants to know why you keep
stopping him from finding love.

356
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:07,880
And with my male friends too.

357
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,360
Yeah. His male friends too.

358
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,240
Why do you keep haunting
the men who get close to him

359
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:15,120
until he has no one left?

360
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,520
No friends.

361
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:17,800
And his boyfriends left him.

362
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,600
You don't have to rub it in.

363
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,240
Stay quiet.

364
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:25,200
I'll kill you!

365
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:26,840
Okay.

366
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:28,640
If you want to kill me, go ahead.

367
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,280
But let me hear your reason first.

368
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:32,160
Why do you keep tormenting Rakkhun?

369
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:34,200
Aren't you his ancestor?

370
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:36,080
I'm not tormenting him.

371
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:39,000
I'm protecting him from bad people.

372
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:44,320
Someday, he'll understand.

373
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,240
Understand what?

374
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,360
Are you delusional?

375
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:50,280
You're traumatizing him.

376
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:54,080
He's afraid to live his life
or even let himself be happy.

377
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:57,280
Now I understand
why you haven't been reincarnated.

378
00:21:57,360 --> 00:22:00,600
It's because you're this kind of ghost
that you're stuck here like--

379
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:04,400
Vann!

380
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:13,360
Garlah! Don't hurt him!

381
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:15,880
Garlah! Stop it right now!

382
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:19,320
Garlah! Please stop!

383
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:23,080
Garlah! Stop it! Enough!

384
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,640
I'm begging you.

385
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,400
Please stop.

386
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:39,080
Vann! Are you hurt?

387
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,520
Are you okay?

388
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:10,640
Don't worry about it.

389
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:12,080
I'm fine.

390
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,680
This is nothing. She can't hurt me.

391
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:19,400
Tonight, I'm going back to sleep
at my condo.

392
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,600
And I'm going to cancel the job.

393
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:24,000
I'll talk to Linda myself.

394
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,280
Why are you canceling?

395
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:29,600
Rakkhun.

396
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:32,120
Garlah finally talked to me.

397
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:33,560
Just give me some time.

398
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,560
Every time Garlah appears,

399
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,400
you always get hurt.

400
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:41,040
Do you have to get your neck broken
before this job can end?

401
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,680
I can't be responsible for your life.

402
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:46,560
You don't have to be responsible for me.

403
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:48,160
I chose to take this job.

404
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:50,000
When the job's done, I get paid.

405
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:51,600
See? It's a win-win for both of us.

406
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:54,720
Do you want the money that badly?

407
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:59,720
You want money so badly that you don't
even care about your own life?

408
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:03,720
Yeah.

409
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:05,680
I want the money.

410
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:07,840
Or I wouldn't have taken this job.

411
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:13,840
I'll pay you the full fee.

412
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:17,080
And we don't have to see each other again.

413
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:19,360
I'm ending the job here.

414
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:28,080
Rakkhun, wait.

415
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,080
This isn't how you solve the problem.

416
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:33,560
You know Garlah will show up again
if you have a boyfriend.

417
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,560
Forget it.

418
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:38,960
If it's that difficult,
then I just won't have one.

419
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:42,680
I won't die just because
I don't have love in my life.

420
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:08,200
<i>Let me whisper softly</i>

421
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:26,040
<i>Where are you?</i>

422
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:27,520
<i>Everyone’s waiting</i>
<i>in the music rehearsal room.</i>

423
00:25:30,080 --> 00:25:31,640
<i>You guys go ahead and practice.</i>

424
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:32,840
<i>I’ll catch up with you later.</i>

425
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:35,920
TONHON

426
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:57,040
I'm not trying to pressure you.

427
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:00,560
It's just that the email
said the result was still pending.

428
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:03,920
So I came to ask
if you've made a decision yet.

429
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:06,200
I haven't thought about it yet.

430
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:08,360
I have a lot of other things to do.

431
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:10,200
Excuse me.

432
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:11,680
Wait.

433
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:14,160
You should back off

434
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:16,800
before I reject your offer.

435
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:36,640
I heard you want to apply
to be a singer here.

436
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:38,160
Yes.

437
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:40,120
You can audition me first.

438
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:42,280
I can play guitar. I can dance.

439
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:44,400
I can definitely entertain
the customers here.

440
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:46,320
I guarantee they won't get bored.

441
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:53,200
I suppose this is one way
for you to convince Phatee

442
00:26:53,280 --> 00:26:54,920
to take your job, right?

443
00:26:58,440 --> 00:27:01,680
To be honest, customers…

444
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,240
I want them too.

445
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:08,000
But I'm really not sure
if the money I'd spend on you

446
00:27:08,720 --> 00:27:11,440
would be worth what I'd get in return.

447
00:27:13,600 --> 00:27:15,000
Then…

448
00:27:16,720 --> 00:27:18,240
what if you didn't have to pay me?

449
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:21,240
I'm willing to sing here for free.

450
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:24,280
As long as I get to sing with Phatee.

451
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:30,760
- For free?
- Yes.

452
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:35,160
Deal.

453
00:27:51,760 --> 00:27:53,200
We're closed.

454
00:27:57,520 --> 00:28:02,320
Sitting here from opening until
closing like this isn't going to work.

455
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:03,920
I'm not taking your job no matter what.

456
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:06,800
Today, I'm here as a customer of the bar.

457
00:28:07,320 --> 00:28:09,760
Or if you change your mind,
you can tell me.

458
00:28:10,520 --> 00:28:11,560
No way.

459
00:28:39,720 --> 00:28:41,040
Kind.

460
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:42,280
Warm.

461
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:44,200
Caring.

462
00:28:44,280 --> 00:28:45,800
Idealistic.

463
00:28:47,040 --> 00:28:48,760
You have all the traits of a male lead.

464
00:28:50,920 --> 00:28:52,760
You're drunk,
but you're still writing fiction.

465
00:28:53,280 --> 00:28:55,440
Are all writers as delusional as you?

466
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:58,480
I'll take you home.

467
00:28:59,280 --> 00:29:00,480
Stay still for a second.

468
00:29:09,760 --> 00:29:10,760
Can you walk?

469
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,880
Watch where you're going.

470
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:37,200
Hey.

471
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:39,920
What's wrong? Why are you drinking alone?

472
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:43,760
I'm feeling a little down.

473
00:29:44,360 --> 00:29:45,880
I'll turn off the lights.

474
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:58,000
You don't usually drink.

475
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:01,280
Why? Did something bad happen?

476
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:05,400
It's not that bad.

477
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:08,200
Since we're already at it,

478
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:10,120
I might as well ask you.

479
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,480
Go ahead.

480
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,480
Today, I summoned the ghost.

481
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,480
And I talked to her for a bit.

482
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,440
Then the ghost strangled me.

483
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:21,960
Right here.

484
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:26,360
She strangled you pretty hard.

485
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:27,920
So?

486
00:30:28,520 --> 00:30:31,360
You don't want this job
because the ghost strangled you?

487
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:33,400
No.

488
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:35,040
I want to keep going.

489
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:37,600
But Rakkhun wants to cancel.

490
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:39,840
I seriously don't get it.

491
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,040
I followed the entire brief

492
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,720
so I could finish
the job as fast as possible.

493
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:48,600
But suddenly today, Rakkhun got mad at me.

494
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:50,800
I called, but he didn't answer.

495
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,800
I texted, but he didn't reply.

496
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:55,640
I don't know if he can be alone.

497
00:30:55,720 --> 00:30:57,360
He's already such a scaredy-cat.

498
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:00,400
And he's been studying hard lately.

499
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:03,000
He hasn't been sleeping well.

500
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:05,360
If he gets sick,
who's going to take care of him?

501
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:10,600
Rakkhun is probably worried about you.

502
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,400
Just like you're worried about Rakkhun.

503
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,000
I'm not worried about him.

504
00:31:14,080 --> 00:31:15,680
I'm more worried about my money.

505
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,280
You're afraid he won't be able to sleep.

506
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:22,760
You're afraid he'll see the ghost?

507
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:23,840
You're worried about the money?

508
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:26,520
You're worried about him.

509
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:27,840
You just won't admit it.

510
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:39,960
Ask yourself how you really feel,
then go talk to him.

511
00:31:40,040 --> 00:31:42,800
There's no point sitting here
sad and drinking beer.

512
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:44,120
It's just a waste of beer.

513
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:50,920
I'll take it, then.

514
00:32:42,040 --> 00:32:44,680
VANN

515
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,080
VANN: CAN I TALK TO YOU FOR A MOMENT?

516
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:57,480
<i>Can I talk to you for a moment?</i>

517
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:00,240
- Hello.
- Which one's yours?

518
00:33:00,320 --> 00:33:01,600
- This one.
- Okay.

519
00:33:03,920 --> 00:33:05,160
- This one's yours, right?
- Yeah.

520
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:06,800
It's a semi-detached house.

521
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:09,320
It's nice. Not bad.

522
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,360
Thanks.

523
00:33:13,040 --> 00:33:15,840
- Yay!
- Yay!

524
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:17,600
Our group is so good. We all got A's.

525
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,680
Yeah.

526
00:33:18,760 --> 00:33:19,640
What do you guys say?

527
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:21,120
Should we celebrate tonight?

528
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,880
You're acting like we've graduated.

529
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:25,040
Come on.

530
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:28,400
People who want to drink
can always find a reason to drink.

531
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:30,520
So, what do you guys say? Who's going?

532
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:32,000
- So I can book a table.
- I'm in.

533
00:33:32,080 --> 00:33:33,280
- Me too.
- You guys in the back, you coming?

534
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:34,800
- I'm in.
- Me too.

535
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:36,440
Let's drink!

536
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,720
Okay, I'm in.

537
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:39,800
Okay.

538
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:42,480
And Rakkhun, are you coming?

539
00:33:51,600 --> 00:33:52,600
Come with us.

540
00:33:53,120 --> 00:33:55,520
I want you to come too.

541
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:56,960
We haven't had drinks together in ages.

542
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:01,040
It's fun when a bunch of us go together.

543
00:34:03,960 --> 00:34:05,160
Okay, I'll come too.

544
00:34:05,760 --> 00:34:07,760
Fabulous!

545
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:10,120
We're going drinking tonight!

546
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:12,239
- Book us a table.
- Let's celebrate!

547
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,560
<i>These are noodles from my shop.</i>

548
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:19,440
I don't know if there's
enough for everyone.

549
00:34:19,960 --> 00:34:21,480
This is a lot.
There's definitely enough for everyone.

550
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:23,080
Thank you so much.

551
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:26,199
Vann's here just in time.

552
00:34:26,280 --> 00:34:29,360
Then, I'll get going.

553
00:34:29,440 --> 00:34:31,040
- I'll go check on the shop.
- Sure.

554
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,040
Make yourself at home.

555
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:33,280
Thank you so much.

556
00:34:38,719 --> 00:34:40,679
What's with that hair color?

557
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:42,520
We haven't seen each other in a year.

558
00:34:42,600 --> 00:34:44,280
Shouldn't you ask how I've been?

559
00:34:44,360 --> 00:34:46,239
And you're asking about my hair color?

560
00:34:46,840 --> 00:34:48,600
I brought you some noodles.

561
00:34:48,679 --> 00:34:50,320
I saw there were a lot of people here,

562
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,880
so I brought a bunch of bags.

563
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:54,040
Thanks.

564
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:56,800
That's it?

565
00:34:58,440 --> 00:34:59,640
Hey.

566
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,280
I'm seriously asking you.

567
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:03,120
What's better about
this place than our home?

568
00:35:03,200 --> 00:35:04,760
Why won't you come home?

569
00:35:05,440 --> 00:35:06,600
You want me to come back?

570
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:08,120
But you're the one who kicked me out.

571
00:35:08,200 --> 00:35:11,600
How was I supposed to know
you'd actually leave?

572
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:13,800
I said it in the heat of the moment.

573
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:15,400
Couldn't you tell?

574
00:35:16,040 --> 00:35:17,240
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

575
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:20,840
I'm going to a funeral nearby,
so I stopped by to see you.

576
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:22,480
Whose funeral?

577
00:35:22,560 --> 00:35:24,240
Aunt Nid's.

578
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:25,440
She had cancer.

579
00:35:25,520 --> 00:35:27,680
She died not long after she was diagnosed.

580
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:29,720
Aunt Nid is a relative on Dad's side.

581
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,080
Then why didn't Dad come too?

582
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:34,360
Your dad didn't get along with Aunt Nid.

583
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:36,920
I didn't want other people
gossiping about us,

584
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:39,200
so I just went to get it over with.

585
00:35:39,280 --> 00:35:41,640
Let people say whatever they want, Mom.

586
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:43,200
Even Buddha was gossiped about.

587
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:45,960
Wow, you dare lecture me, Vann?

588
00:35:46,040 --> 00:35:48,160
Okay, enough about this.

589
00:35:49,680 --> 00:35:52,440
Right, I've saved enough
to study abroad now.

590
00:35:52,960 --> 00:35:54,600
If I finish this job, I can go right away.

591
00:35:55,240 --> 00:35:57,240
You really want to go study, right?

592
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:59,200
You're not going just to spite me, right?

593
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,080
I really want to go.

594
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:02,640
It's my dream.

595
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:08,120
Then I'd better get to the funeral.

596
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,320
I'm leaving.

597
00:36:11,080 --> 00:36:12,200
I'll see you off.

598
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:15,480
No need. I can go by myself.

599
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:17,520
Focus on your work.

600
00:36:27,640 --> 00:36:28,480
Vann.

601
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:31,760
How's your job going?

602
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:36,360
I heard you had a fight with the client.

603
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:38,520
Did Rakkhun come to
cancel the job with you?

604
00:36:39,120 --> 00:36:40,280
He came to talk to me.

605
00:36:40,800 --> 00:36:43,120
But he hasn't officially canceled yet.

606
00:36:44,640 --> 00:36:46,280
Go sort things out with him properly.

607
00:36:47,040 --> 00:36:48,680
Don't let it become a problem.

608
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:03,560
Here's your drink.

609
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:05,080
Thirsty, huh?

610
00:37:05,160 --> 00:37:07,560
- You chugged that down fast.
- Two glasses now.

611
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:08,840
The beer's here.

612
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:13,160
Why hasn't Linda dropped
this supplier already?

613
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:16,120
Other people need it too.

614
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,280
Hey.

615
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:20,680
Why are you complaining?

616
00:37:20,760 --> 00:37:23,200
You'll have to work together
someday anyway, right?

617
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:25,560
You two should get along.

618
00:37:25,640 --> 00:37:27,080
There's no need, Mimi.

619
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:30,720
Actually, we already know
each other very well.

620
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:33,200
Because I know him so well,

621
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:34,680
I don't want to know him anymore.

622
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:36,320
Know each other well?

623
00:37:39,120 --> 00:37:40,520
Here's the beer bill.

624
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:45,360
I'll take care of this bill.

625
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:46,920
By the way,

626
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:51,200
you two have known each other
for a long time, right?

627
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,160
You know him that well?

628
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:55,400
And you know him so well
you don't want to know him…

629
00:37:55,480 --> 00:37:57,240
You two are exes, aren't you?

630
00:37:57,320 --> 00:37:58,240
Mimi!

631
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:01,520
You could say that.

632
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:06,000
Actually, it started
with us being friends.

633
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:18,000
Thank you so much for today.

634
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:19,800
I'm chill.

635
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:23,280
I'm glad you agreed to go drinking.

636
00:38:25,440 --> 00:38:27,440
Going once in a while is fun too.

637
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:30,760
Rakkhun.

638
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:33,200
Can I ask you something?

639
00:38:34,640 --> 00:38:37,280
I don't know if I can ask you this.

640
00:38:38,080 --> 00:38:39,240
But I want to know,

641
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:42,760
the guy who picked you up
at the faculty building that day,

642
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:44,120
who is he?

643
00:38:47,680 --> 00:38:48,800
He's an older guy I know.

644
00:38:51,640 --> 00:38:52,680
An older guy?

645
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:56,520
I know everyone in your life.

646
00:38:57,120 --> 00:38:59,640
You're not someone who lets
just anyone into your life.

647
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:05,440
I'll be straight with you.

648
00:39:07,280 --> 00:39:08,800
You've moved on from me, right?

649
00:39:09,440 --> 00:39:10,760
So I can come to terms with it.

650
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:13,440
It's not like that.

651
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:15,440
It's complicated.

652
00:39:16,040 --> 00:39:18,000
We're not seeing each other or anything.

653
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:22,280
That means I still have a chance, right?

654
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:29,920
I think you should move on.

655
00:39:32,200 --> 00:39:34,400
Let's each go live our own lives.

656
00:39:39,680 --> 00:39:41,040
If you're saying this because

657
00:39:41,120 --> 00:39:42,760
you don't feel anything for me anymore,

658
00:39:43,720 --> 00:39:44,800
I'll leave you alone.

659
00:39:46,160 --> 00:39:48,560
But if you're just afraid
the ghost will haunt me again,

660
00:39:49,240 --> 00:39:50,760
I'm not going anywhere.

661
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:54,240
I won't let the ghost ruin
our relationship again.

662
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:10,280
I told you to get out of Rakkhun's life!

663
00:40:15,680 --> 00:40:16,720
Kan, what's wrong?

664
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:20,240
I'm fine.

665
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,360
I'm not afraid of ghosts.

666
00:40:23,720 --> 00:40:25,560
I'm more afraid of not being with you.

667
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:38,000
Kan!

668
00:40:43,400 --> 00:40:44,840
Stop! Garlah!

669
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:46,320
I told you to stop!

670
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:47,960
Stop hurting people.

671
00:40:51,880 --> 00:40:54,000
Garlah! Stop hurting people.

672
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,040
I warned you.

673
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:57,200
You didn't listen to me!

674
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:59,720
You'll fucking destroy
yourself over a man!

675
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:02,040
- Sicko!
- Rakkhun!

676
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:24,080
I think you should go home.

677
00:41:30,840 --> 00:41:31,880
Are you okay?

678
00:41:34,400 --> 00:41:35,480
I'm okay.

679
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,600
Go shower and get some sleep.

680
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:45,000
I'll head home now

681
00:41:45,080 --> 00:41:46,040
so you can get some rest.

682
00:41:47,240 --> 00:41:48,600
Wait.

683
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:55,920
Can you stay with me tonight?

684
00:42:00,680 --> 00:42:03,320
Hey, can I ask you something?

685
00:42:04,160 --> 00:42:05,760
What are you going to do with the money?

686
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:07,720
I want to study in Japan.

687
00:42:08,640 --> 00:42:11,600
Believe it or not,
I graduated with a gold medal.

688
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:13,520
And when I was an undergrad,

689
00:42:14,120 --> 00:42:15,880
I got a full scholarship too.

690
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:19,160
Big companies were fighting over me
before I even graduated.

691
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:21,720
Then why don't you apply
for a scholarship?

692
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:23,240
With a profile this good,

693
00:42:23,840 --> 00:42:24,760
it shouldn't be that hard, right?

694
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:27,160
I already took the exam.

695
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,040
It was a full scholarship too.

696
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,400
Only one person
in the whole country gets it.

697
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:33,760
I was so damn confident during the exam.

698
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:35,360
I thought I'd definitely get it.

699
00:42:35,440 --> 00:42:38,480
You know, my whole life,

700
00:42:38,560 --> 00:42:40,080
I'd never failed an exam before.

701
00:42:40,160 --> 00:42:41,800
Until this scholarship exam.

702
00:42:44,200 --> 00:42:45,280
And I found out later that

703
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:48,720
the person who got the scholarship
fucking got it through connections.

704
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:51,120
So I decided to earn the money myself.

705
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:53,000
I'm not counting on those
scholarships anymore.

706
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:55,040
You're amazing.

707
00:42:55,120 --> 00:42:56,160
If it were me,

708
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:57,560
I'd have given up already.

709
00:42:58,240 --> 00:43:01,040
Hey, Vann, I think
I heard Garlah just now too.

710
00:43:01,840 --> 00:43:03,520
What did Garlah say to you?

711
00:43:05,440 --> 00:43:09,280
Garlah said my life
would be ruined because of a man.

712
00:43:10,480 --> 00:43:11,480
Obviously.

713
00:43:12,160 --> 00:43:14,400
Garlah doesn't like you dating men.

714
00:43:14,920 --> 00:43:16,880
She's so fucking conservative.

715
00:43:17,640 --> 00:43:18,920
That's possible.

716
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,520
Go to sleep. It's late.

717
00:43:41,120 --> 00:43:42,320
Can I hold your hand?

718
00:43:43,360 --> 00:43:44,520
It'll put me at ease.

719
00:44:04,480 --> 00:44:05,680
You can sleep here.

720
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:07,120
I don't mind.

721
00:45:08,120 --> 00:45:09,320
Talay.

722
00:45:22,080 --> 00:45:24,320
Have you seen Talay? Isn't he here?

723
00:45:26,240 --> 00:45:27,880
He went out.

724
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:28,880
What is it?

725
00:45:33,880 --> 00:45:34,920
Well,

726
00:45:36,120 --> 00:45:37,640
I don't know who to talk to.

727
00:45:38,880 --> 00:45:40,200
Talay isn't here either.

728
00:45:40,720 --> 00:45:42,200
This might sound a little weird,

729
00:45:42,280 --> 00:45:46,680
but have you ever liked someone
or ever loved someone?

730
00:45:50,840 --> 00:45:52,600
- I have.
- Who?

731
00:45:54,280 --> 00:45:55,680
I mean,

732
00:45:56,440 --> 00:45:57,760
what does it feel like?

733
00:45:59,560 --> 00:46:00,560
Who do you like, then?

734
00:46:01,360 --> 00:46:03,920
- Rakkhun?
- Are you crazy?

735
00:46:04,840 --> 00:46:06,200
Just someone.

736
00:46:07,160 --> 00:46:09,240
I'm still not sure, so I came to ask.

737
00:46:12,280 --> 00:46:16,000
I was interested, curious, and restless.

738
00:46:16,800 --> 00:46:18,160
I couldn't stop thinking about him.

739
00:46:18,680 --> 00:46:19,720
That's how I knew I liked him.

740
00:46:23,960 --> 00:46:26,960
Do you feel anything strange
when you're around him?

741
00:46:27,720 --> 00:46:28,720
Like,

742
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:31,280
sleeping well,

743
00:46:31,800 --> 00:46:33,800
sometimes getting butterflies
in your stomach,

744
00:46:33,880 --> 00:46:36,000
or feeling a flutter in your chest.

745
00:46:37,160 --> 00:46:39,080
Your arms and legs never
seem to know where to go.

746
00:46:39,920 --> 00:46:41,240
It depends on the person.

747
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:43,960
How do you feel when you're around him?

748
00:46:52,240 --> 00:46:54,000
Before I sleep, I think about him.

749
00:46:54,720 --> 00:46:56,200
When I wake up, I think about him.

750
00:46:57,280 --> 00:46:59,240
I expect every notification
to be his message.

751
00:47:00,720 --> 00:47:02,520
I like seeing him smile.

752
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:07,200
I want to smack myself
for saying things that hurt him.

753
00:47:08,520 --> 00:47:10,520
When he can't sleep, I can't sleep either.

754
00:47:12,280 --> 00:47:14,200
When he's sad, I'm sad too.

755
00:47:15,760 --> 00:47:17,400
If his eyes well up,

756
00:47:17,960 --> 00:47:19,400
I feel like I'm going crazy.

757
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:22,880
I'm angry at myself
for not being able to do anything.

758
00:47:23,920 --> 00:47:26,040
I want to be close to him,
but I can't be too close.

759
00:47:28,200 --> 00:47:29,760
Is this normal?

760
00:47:31,240 --> 00:47:32,960
Do you feel that way about me?

761
00:47:33,560 --> 00:47:34,760
About you?

762
00:47:35,280 --> 00:47:36,560
No way.

763
00:47:37,160 --> 00:47:38,680
That means that person is special to you.

764
00:47:40,160 --> 00:47:43,400
This is what having a crush
on someone feels like.

765
00:48:01,960 --> 00:48:02,880
Rakkhun.

766
00:48:06,800 --> 00:48:07,920
I bought this for you.

767
00:48:08,560 --> 00:48:09,720
Thanks.

768
00:48:12,280 --> 00:48:14,640
I think you should stay away
from me for now.

769
00:48:15,840 --> 00:48:17,280
You'll get hurt again.

770
00:48:17,360 --> 00:48:18,640
No.

771
00:48:19,160 --> 00:48:20,640
I want to be close to you.

772
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:23,080
I'm not afraid of that ghost anymore.

773
00:48:24,040 --> 00:48:25,240
Look.

774
00:48:28,640 --> 00:48:30,400
I've got something powerful too.

775
00:48:30,480 --> 00:48:31,880
Whatever ghost it is, bring it on.

776
00:48:31,960 --> 00:48:32,800
I'm not afraid.

777
00:48:33,560 --> 00:48:34,720
I told you.

778
00:48:35,240 --> 00:48:36,840
I'm not leaving you again.

779
00:48:54,680 --> 00:48:56,000
Whoa.

780
00:48:56,080 --> 00:48:57,800
You look so handsome today.

781
00:48:57,880 --> 00:48:58,840
Like a model.

782
00:48:58,920 --> 00:49:00,360
Where are you going to model?

783
00:49:00,440 --> 00:49:02,240
I'm here to take you back to the condo.

784
00:49:02,960 --> 00:49:04,480
And then I'll take you out to eat.

785
00:49:04,560 --> 00:49:06,400
I happened to get a voucher.

786
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:08,000
It's a Michelin restaurant.

787
00:49:09,520 --> 00:49:11,440
I have a study session with friends.

788
00:49:12,600 --> 00:49:15,160
By the way, I can still save
this voucher for later, right?

789
00:49:16,840 --> 00:49:18,000
Sure.

790
00:49:18,760 --> 00:49:20,080
Want me to pick you up?

791
00:49:20,600 --> 00:49:21,440
Where are you studying?

792
00:49:25,480 --> 00:49:26,720
At my house.

793
00:49:27,480 --> 00:49:29,240
I'll pick him up and drop him off myself.

794
00:49:29,840 --> 00:49:31,240
I'll take good care of him.

795
00:49:34,080 --> 00:49:35,160
You don't have to worry.

796
00:49:35,240 --> 00:49:36,200
I'll let you know when I get there.

797
00:49:38,880 --> 00:49:39,760
Take good care of yourself.

798
00:49:39,840 --> 00:49:42,440
Okay. I'm going.

799
00:50:06,600 --> 00:50:07,880
Garlah, where are you?

800
00:50:07,960 --> 00:50:09,240
Come out and talk to me.

801
00:50:10,440 --> 00:50:11,480
You don't have to hide.

802
00:50:11,560 --> 00:50:13,840
You can come into my dreams
almost every night,

803
00:50:13,920 --> 00:50:15,440
so just coming out to talk

804
00:50:15,520 --> 00:50:16,920
